### Default icon

Without `color`, an icon inherits its parent's foreground. This preserves button and link state colours.

```jsx
<FaceHappyIcon />
```

### Icon sizes

```jsx
<Fragment>
  <ComponentTitle>All sizes</ComponentTitle>
  <FaceHappyIcon size="xsmall" />
  <WalkIcon size="small" /> <WatchIcon size="medium" />
  <HeadsetIcon size="large" /> <AndroidIcon size="xlarge" />
  <ComponentTitle>Responsive</ComponentTitle>
  <AndroidIcon size={{ initial: 'small', md: 'medium', lg: 'large', xl: 'xlarge' }} />
</Fragment>
```

### Icon color

Semantic colour props select the matching `icon-*` token for the active brand and mode. `body`, `heading` and `link` are also available. Existing colours without an icon-token counterpart, such as `pop` and faint variants, retain their previous mappings for compatibility.

```tsx
() => {
  const ALL_COLORS = [
    'body',
    'heading',
    'muted',
    'primary',
    'hero',
    'holler',
    'link',
    'success',
    'info',
    'warning',
    'danger',
    'system-error',
    'mono',
    'reversed',
  ] as const;

  return (
    <div className="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2">
      {ALL_COLORS.map(color => (
        <div key={color} className="flex flex-col items-center gap-1 w-14">
          <div className={color === 'mono' || color === 'reversed' ? 'bg-surface-hero p-1' : 'p-1'}>
            <TickCircleIcon color={color} />
          </div>
          <p className="typography-body-11 text-text-body text-center">{color}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};
```
